%I A401778 #5 Nov 05 2026 23:07:21
%S A401778 3,74,1294,30244,219632,1550455,9547456
%N A401778 Number of free polyhexes with 3n cells that can be trisected into three congruent polyhexes.
%C A401778 Here congruent means equal up to rotation, reflection and translation, so the two halves may be mirror images of each other. We call such a polyhex "trisectable".
